# Trivy ignore list — keep this list minimal and document each entry.
# Each line is a CVE or GHSA identifier; a `# reason:` comment line above
# documents why it's safe to defer the fix.

# rustls-webpki 0.101.7 — DoS via panic on malformed CRL BIT STRING.
# This version is pulled transitively by livekit-api 0.4.14 → tokio-tungstenite
# 0.20 → rustls 0.21, none of which we can upgrade without livekit-api
# itself moving past rustls 0.21. Fixed series (0.103.13+) IS used by
# reqwest 0.12 elsewhere in the tree (we already track that).
# Risk assessment: the panic only fires when the TLS layer parses a CRL.
# Our LiveKit connections do not exercise CRL parsing (LiveKit servers do
# not serve CRLs; standard cert chain validation only). Re-evaluate when
# livekit-api > 0.4.14 ships against rustls >= 0.23.
GHSA-82j2-j2ch-gfr8
